# {{ m }}

This directory contains a self-contained C++98 wrapper with a C99 execution core. Put your application in `app.cpp`; regenerate the machine files from the DSL when model behavior changes. The generated program has no Python or third-party runtime dependency.

**Generated files:** Use `machine.hpp` and `MachineWrapper` for integration. `machine.c` and `machine.cpp` are generated implementation files. This guide and `README_zh.md` describe the same API. The native machine type behind the wrapper is opaque statically sized storage: read it only through the wrapper. {% if model.has_regions %}This model declares regions, so it has no single current state; read its position as a configuration value.{% else %}This model declares no regions, so its position is always one current state.{% endif %} Follow [Quick Start](#quick-start), then [Integration](#integration), [Recovery](#recovery), [Configuration values](#configuration) and [Build](#build).

